Formula 1 coverage on Apple TV is set to be broadcast in Dolby Atmos beginning later this month.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/10/Apple-exclusive-F1-partner.jpg" alt="" width="3840" height="2160" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1023659" /><br/>
Starting with the U.S. Grand Prix weekend on Friday, October 23 in Austin, Texas, Formula 1 coverage on Apple TV will be available in Dolby Atmos on supported devices.<br/>
<br/>
Apple says the introduction of Dolby Atmos will create a more immersive presentation designed to put viewers at the center of the race. The Atmos mix will encompass team radio, commentary, engines, on-track battles, and activity in the pit lane.<br/>
<br/>
The combination of Dolby Vision and Dolby Atmos is intended to capture the full audiovisual intensity of Formula 1 and bring viewers closer to the action, according to Apple.<br/>
<br/>
Oliver Schusser – Apple's VP of music, sports, Apple TV and Beats – spoke to <em><a href="https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/digital/apple-dolby-atmos-live-formula-1-coverage-races-1236722280/">The Hollywood Reporter</a></em> about the new presentation:<br/>
<blockquote>"If you are a sports fan today, our viewpoint is that the experience is – I'm going to be polite and say not easy. There really has not been a lot of innovation. We went into sports a couple of years back with the intention to make a difference for the customer, and this is a continuation of that journey."</blockquote>"The sound is what makes it emotional; it is the sound that guides you through that and builds the tension," said John Couling, senior VP of entertainment for Dolby Laboratories, speaking to <em>THR</em>. "That is what Dolby Atmos will deliver."<br/>
<br/>
The Atmos presentation works on supported Apple devices and compatible Dolby-enabled TVs, soundbars, and home-theater systems.<br/>
 <br/>
